# Packages the live edition leaves out of the official live system's list (OMABOOT_FLAVOUR=live,
# builder/build-iso.sh). The live edition has no installer and no rescue toolbox: these are the
# installer's, disk imaging, VM guest agents, VPN and dial-up clients, network tools, and the
# accessibility speech and braille daemons (the tester can only be used by looking at the screen;
# owner, 2026-10-14). Dependencies nothing else needs (Python, Perl's extras) go with them; pacman
# resolves that, so nothing still installed loses a dependency. The release's difference report
# explains each (builder/omaboot/release/explain.tsv). nbd stays: the initramfs's PXE hook needs
# nbd-client to build.
archinstall
brltty
clonezilla
cloud-init
darkhttpd
espeakup
fsarchiver
git
hyperv
irssi
lftp
linux-atm
linux-firmware-marvell
livecd-sounds
lynx
man-db
man-pages
mc
memtest86+
memtest86+-efi
nmap
open-iscsi
open-vm-tools
openconnect
openvpn
partclone
partimage
pptpclient
qemu-guest-agent
reflector
refind
sof-firmware
virtualbox-guest-utils-nox
vpnc
wvdial
xl2tpd
